    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Permit" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Court permits witness to give evidence by video link." ;
    cml:premiseText "None" ;
    cml:conclusionText "None" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-279-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "279 2  When court may take evidence by video link" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "In a proceeding, the court may, on application by a party to the proceeding, direct that a witness give evidence by video link if:  (a) the witness will give the evidence from outside Australia; and  (b) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and  (c) the facilities required by section 279.3 are available or can reasonably be made available; and  (d) the court is satisfied that attendance of the witness at the court to give the evidence would:  Schedule 2  Supporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings" ;
    cof:pageNumber "25"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "279 3  Technical requirements for video link"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-279-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A witness can give evidence under a direction only if:  (a) the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is sitting (the Australian location); and  (b) the place where the evidence is given (the overseas location); are equipped with video facilities that:  (c) enable appropriate persons at the Australian location to see and hear the witness give the evidence; and  (d) enable appropriate persons at the overseas location to see and hear appropriate persons at the Australian location.  (2) In subsection (1): appropriate persons means such persons as the court considers appropriate." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A witness can give evidence under a direction only if:  (a) the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is sitting (the Australian location); and  (b) the place where the evidence is given (the overseas location); are equipped with video facilities that:  (c) enable appropriate persons at the Australian location to see and hear the witness give the evidence; and  (d) enable appropriate persons at the overseas location to see and hear appropriate persons at the Australian location.  (2) In subsection (1): appropriate persons means such persons as the court considers appropriate."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "092d44c60dc2f6d02dd133312052e9a9cc344a34360ec4589307af91bedcf927" ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-3-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-3-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2018c00199.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2018c00199.pdf, p.26" .
doc:sch-2-sec-279-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "279 3  Technical requirements for video link" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A witness can give evidence under a direction only if:  (a) the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is sitting (the Australian location); and  (b) the place where the evidence is given (the overseas location); are equipped with video facilities that:  (c) enable appropriate persons at the Australian location to see and hear the witness give the evidence; and  (d) enable appropriate persons at the overseas location to see and hear appropriate persons at the Australian location.  (2) In subsection (1): appropriate persons means such persons as the court considers appropriate." ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer .

