concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "279 4  Application of laws about witnesses"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-279-4 ;
    values:originalText "A person who gives evidence under a direction is taken to give it at the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is sitting. Note: This section has effect, for example, for the purposes of laws relating to evidence, procedure, contempt of court and perjury." ;
    skos:definition "A person who gives evidence under a direction is taken to give it at the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is sitting. Note: This section has effect, for example, for the purposes of laws relating to evidence, procedure, contempt of court and perjury."@en ;
