doc:sch-2-sec-16ab-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "16AB(7) Matters relating to victim impact statements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) For the purposes of Part IAD (about protecting vulnerable persons):  (a) giving evidence includes giving a reading under subsection (4); and  (b) a cross-examination includes a cross-examination under subsection (6). Note: This confirms that any protections available under Part IAD will be available for the reading or the cross-examination.  Supporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings  Schedule 2 Application of amendments  Part 3  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness Protection and Other Measures) Act 2013 Compilation date: 23/5/18 Registered: 30/5/18" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-93 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "93 Application of amendments"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-93 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The amendments made by this Schedule apply in relation to offences committed (or alleged to have been committed) on or after the day this Schedule commences. (2) The amendments made by Part 1 of this Schedule also apply in relation to proceedings instituted after the commencement of Schedule 5 to the Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018 (whether the proceedings are for offences committed, or alleged to have been committed, before or after the commencement of this Schedule).  Schedule 3  Deterring people smuggling" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The amendments made by this Schedule apply in relation to offences committed (or alleged to have been committed) on or after the day this Schedule commences. (2) The amendments made by Part 1 of this Schedule also apply in relation to proceedings instituted after the commencement of Schedule 5 to the Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018 (whether the proceedings are for offences committed, or alleged to have been committed, before or after the commencement of this Schedule).  Schedule 3  Deterring people smuggling"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0580a23e4b28315a50172c29f2c84d0e87637e5ce839f1b797e9950c95e0f9bb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Amendments apply in relation to offences committed on or after the commencement of this Schedule." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
