doc:sch-3-sec-236a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "236A No discharge without conviction for certain offences" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The court may only make an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 (discharge of offenders without conviction) in respect of a charge for an offence against section 233B, 233C or 234A if the person charged was aged under 18 when the offence was alleged to have been committed. Note: See also section 236D, which relates to age." ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 At the end of Subdivision A of Division 12 of Part 2"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-4 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  Deterring people smuggling  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness Protection and Other Measures) Act 2013 Compilation date: 23/5/18 Registered: 30/5/18  236C  Time in immigration detention counts for sentencing etc.  (1) This section applies to the court when imposing a sentence on, or setting a non-parole period for, a person convicted of an offence against this Subdivision.  (2) The court must take into account any period that the person has spent in immigration detention during the period:  (a) starting when the offence was committed; and  (b) ending when the person is sentenced for the offence. Note: This enables the court to take into account time spent while not in punitive detention.  (3) Neither section 236B nor this section prevents section 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 from applying to the imposition of the sentence or the setting of the non-parole period. Note: Section 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 applies State law to aspects of sentencing for federal offences, subject to specified exceptions." ;
    skos:definition "Add:  Deterring people smuggling  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness Protection and Other Measures) Act 2013 Compilation date: 23/5/18 Registered: 30/5/18  236C  Time in immigration detention counts for sentencing etc.  (1) This section applies to the court when imposing a sentence on, or setting a non-parole period for, a person convicted of an offence against this Subdivision.  (2) The court must take into account any period that the person has spent in immigration detention during the period:  (a) starting when the offence was committed; and  (b) ending when the person is sentenced for the offence. Note: This enables the court to take into account time spent while not in punitive detention.  (3) Neither section 236B nor this section prevents section 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 from applying to the imposition of the sentence or the setting of the non-parole period. Note: Section 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 applies State law to aspects of sentencing for federal offences, subject to specified exceptions."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "41db9532d403f20055bc57e0cbe059d8dfc5662e00a4dc3cc21d0603d25bed8d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2018c00199.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2018c00199.pdf, p.32" .
doc:sch-3-sec-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4 At the end of Subdivision A of Division 12 of Part 2" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Add:  Deterring people smuggling  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness Protection and Other Measures) Act 2013 Compilation date: 23/5/18 Registered: 30/5/18  236C  Time in immigration detention counts for sentencing etc.  (1) This section applies to the court when imposing a sentence on, or setting a non-parole period for, a person convicted of an offence against this Subdivision.  (2) The court must take into account any period that the person has spent in immigration detention during the period:  (a) starting when the offence was committed; and  (b) ending when the person is sentenced for the offence. Note: This enables the court to take into account time spent while not in punitive detention.  (3) Neither section 236B nor this section prevents section 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 from applying to the imposition of the sentence or the setting of the non-parole period. Note: Section 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 applies State law to aspects of sentencing for federal offences, subject to specified exceptions." ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer .

