concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "236F Evidentiary certificates—procedural matters"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-236f ;
    values:originalText "(1) A certificate issued under subsection 236E(1) must not be admitted in evidence in proceedings for an offence unless:  (a) the person charged with the offence; or  (b) a lawyer who has appeared for the person in those proceedings; has, at least 28 days before the certificate is sought to be so admitted, been given a copy of the certificate together with notice of the intention to produce the certificate as evidence in the proceedings.  (2) If, under section 236E, a certificate is admitted in evidence in proceedings for an offence, the person charged with the offence may require the person who signed the certificate to be:  (a) called as a witness for the prosecution; and  Schedule 3  Deterring people smuggling" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A certificate issued under subsection 236E(1) must not be admitted in evidence in proceedings for an offence unless:  (a) the person charged with the offence; or  (b) a lawyer who has appeared for the person in those proceedings; has, at least 28 days before the certificate is sought to be so admitted, been given a copy of the certificate together with notice of the intention to produce the certificate as evidence in the proceedings.  (2) If, under section 236E, a certificate is admitted in evidence in proceedings for an offence, the person charged with the offence may require the person who signed the certificate to be:  (a) called as a witness for the prosecution; and  Schedule 3  Deterring people smuggling"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "924a345ec662d30927cea97a950677a855cddc697c59ddc3e3c3ab59713a79ff" ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236f-ss-1 ;
