concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-25 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "25 Subsection 145(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-25 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness Protection and Other Measures) Act 2013 Compilation date: 23/5/18 Registered: 30/5/18  (1) The AUSTRAC CEO may, in writing, appoint as an authorised officer for the purposes of this Act:  (a) a member of the staff of AUSTRAC; or  (b) a person whose services are made available to the AUSTRAC CEO under subsection 225(3), other than a person covered by paragraph 225(3)(g). Note: For revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness Protection and Other Measures) Act 2013 Compilation date: 23/5/18 Registered: 30/5/18  (1) The AUSTRAC CEO may, in writing, appoint as an authorised officer for the purposes of this Act:  (a) a member of the staff of AUSTRAC; or  (b) a person whose services are made available to the AUSTRAC CEO under subsection 225(3), other than a person covered by paragraph 225(3)(g). Note: For revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0b825170e60ce2ce5aa1447482dd17ed4499288dc71362dd89d22baba8231c13" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Appoints AUSTRAC staff as authorised officers." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2018c00199.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2018c00199.pdf, p.42" ;
