    skos:definition "(4) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after making a decision under subsection (2), give written notice to the applicant of:  (a) the decision; and  (b) if the decision is to cancel a person’s registration—the date the cancellation takes effect; and  (c) the reasons for the decision; and  (d) a statement setting out particulars of the applicant’s right to have the decision reviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal.  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness Protection and Other Measures) Act 2013 Compilation date: 23/5/18 Registered: 30/5/18"@en ;
